  'Digital Art / New Media',
  'Digital Art / New Media is an advanced studio course in contemporary art practices that use digital tools, code, networks, time-based media, sensors, real-time systems, data, AI, and installation technologies. Students learn to make images, moving works, sound pieces, web-based artworks, generative sketches, interactive prototypes, 3D environments, and exhibition-ready projects while developing historical awareness, critique fluency, ethical judgment, technical resilience, and documentation practices.',
  $digajson${"slug": "digital-art-new-media", "title": "Digital Art / New Media", "description": "Digital Art / New Media is an advanced studio course in contemporary art practices that use digital tools, code, networks, time-based media, sensors, real-time systems, data, AI, and installation technologies. Students learn to make images, moving works, sound pieces, web-based artworks, generative sketches, interactive prototypes, 3D environments, and exhibition-ready projects while developing historical awareness, critique fluency, ethical judgment, technical resilience, and documentation practices.", "topics": [{"id": "5c2494d0-035f-4b31-b1d3-09a4b3eff2c3", "type": "topic", "title": "New Media Art Histories, Concepts, and Studio Critique", "description": "This opening unit gives students a shared language for understanding digital art as an artistic, cultural, and technological practice. It connects studio making to histories of video art, net art, systems art, cyberfeminism, tactical media, interactive installation, and contemporary platform culture.", "children": [{"id": "59c3974f-fc9c-4af7-9c6e-b56455d8f11f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital and new media art lineages", "children": [{"id": "5b360352-d422-49a8-b1b9-2a14a9df9c0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Video art and expanded cinema"}, {"id": "af0af1d2-8d6b-43ac-a9aa-972ffa032924", "type": "concept", "title": "Net.art and browser-based work"}, {"id": "53b4bf30-46ea-4562-8988-8a567ffa44d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybernetic, systems, and generative traditions"}, {"id": "97a06fb0-3ff9-4dce-8eb5-92f3441c6d59", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional critique and tactical media"}], "description": "Students learn how digital practice grows from earlier experiments in photography, video, conceptual art, performance, systems aesthetics, and computer graphics."}, {"id": "be96edd4-9253-4f60-a4d0-a7dfbbd7c3b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical vocabulary for technology and culture", "children": [{"id": "1c4c6eec-5458-4992-b81b-732431466656", "type": "concept", "title": "Interface, database, network, protocol, platform"}, {"id": "61614c5c-2719-4592-bc45-a23f2673874c", "type": "concept", "title": "Simulation, interactivity, immersion, remediation"}, {"id": "0ac1375d-d4c7-4dee-8336-a43abc74f45d", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-internet and platform aesthetics"}, {"id": "56bea24d-70a5-4a05-a3d3-c27ebc65541b", "type": "concept", "title": "Attention, surveillance, labor, and identity"}], "description": "The point is to move beyond tool fluency and ask what digital systems do socially, politically, and aesthetically."}, {"id": "5322a723-2c64-40dc-81e7-73610e07fcbd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Studio critique methods", "children": [{"id": "11cd3ff1-e5fc-40aa-8aba-5da393a93879", "type": "concept", "title": "Description, analysis, interpretation, judgment"}, {"id": "dd8ce1a1-debb-43d2-b834-b73c69372655", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototype critique versus finished-work critique"}, {"id": "2c78e46c-8b97-4a6c-bba3-21f1024d8b3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statements and process documentation"}, {"id": "83d658c6-493a-4f2b-9f0c-0e2c6f240c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectful, evidence-based feedback"}], "description": "Students practice giving and receiving critique that addresses concept, form, experience, craft, accessibility, and technical implementation."}]}, {"id": "9fe36c43-e21f-45fc-81d3-33e2ba50f7e6", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Workflow, File Formats, Color, Resolution, and Archiving", "description": "This unit builds the durable habits that let artists move work across software, screens, projectors, printers, web platforms, and archives without losing quality or meaning.", "children": [{"id": "4867e580-d57a-47c5-97f0-8bb404494f52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital workflow and versioning", "children": [{"id": "ef305c1a-0ce0-4f8c-994a-99fd90deeb36", "type": "concept", "title": "Folder structures and naming conventions"}, {"id": "32616e28-279a-41c9-8980-794dc26bba73", "type": "concept", "title": "Source files versus exports"}, {"id": "17e15002-6720-429f-83c6-3b77ac442f45", "type": "concept", "title": "Version notes and iteration logs"}, {"id": "daa7065e-6fb6-4917-adbc-a6a55cfc0379", "type": "concept", "title": "Backup rules and cloud/local redundancy"}], "description": "Students learn to organize projects so experiments remain reversible, inspectable, and shareable."}, {"id": "38251d44-0299-4345-b03a-8e5cc2c8a3fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resolution, compression, and formats", "children": [{"id": "5b0be1a2-254d-47af-8dd6-1262357c015e", "type": "concept", "title": "Raster and vector files"}, {"id": "59527d82-618f-4ab9-bcdc-8b8e2cb326ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Lossless and lossy compression"}, {"id": "e887b0c3-3a33-472e-b7a6-5a6f8625a043", "type": "concept", "title": "Web, print, projection, and installation exports"}, {"id": "49e159db-6e3b-485a-9715-2913b15e2242", "type": "concept", "title": "Code repositories and packaged projects"}], "description": "The gist is knowing what a file is, what it preserves, and what it throws away."}, {"id": "111ee271-5cfc-4bcc-ac3a-91307a5a87fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color and display management", "children": [{"id": "6717820e-ed13-414f-b630-aaa8bde815ce", "type": "concept", "title": "RGB, CMYK, indexed color, and alpha"}, {"id": "c67d039a-199e-40fe-bb9b-c8925e167355", "type": "concept", "title": "Color profiles and calibration"}, {"id": "694dbf7e-5158-48cd-986a-b3477d032bf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Bit depth and dynamic range"}, {"id": "c1705345-3718-41ff-9a14-ba24cdf6d006", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility and contrast"}], "description": "Students develop practical judgment about how color changes across monitors, projectors, print, and mobile devices."}]}, {"id": "e2db2161-c493-4f34-918b-943e250c84d2", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Imaging, Compositing, and Photographic Manipulation", "description": "This unit treats the digital image as a constructed object. Students learn how to manipulate, composite, repair, distort, and question photographic images while staying alert to ethics and visual evidence.", "children": [{"id": "dd1a4839-89bc-4816-be8b-7a98c8765d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layer-based image construction", "children": [{"id": "827b51eb-1ed5-4c58-a458-38b4a60b05b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Selections and masking"}, {"id": "34f78fae-f8c9-4e7b-ad77-541a9ed015fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Adjustment layers and blending modes"}, {"id": "b1bbfff4-dda8-4124-98a9-c3d2b39e84e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Smart objects and non-destructive edits"}, {"id": "02a8d968-fb13-4737-b71b-8f61e9911301", "type": "concept", "title": "Image cleanup and repair"}], "description": "Students learn how complex images are built through non-destructive layering, masks, selections, and adjustment systems."}, {"id": "6234a6f3-ccd7-46b7-ac1c-e44166217fcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compositing and montage", "children": [{"id": "aa2a659c-e6cb-4160-9ac3-efcfc253b878", "type": "concept", "title": "Perspective matching"}, {"id": "64c3f9c3-72ad-474b-9b95-8c3e55a4051e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and shadow logic"}, {"id": "777f2162-e19a-40c7-b237-5dac1ce872ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture and grain consistency"}, {"id": "e39de29a-662d-4a0d-b114-581e9713c063", "type": "concept", "title": "Surreal, documentary, and speculative montage"}], "description": "The goal is to build convincing or deliberately unstable visual worlds through scale, light, color, and perspective."}, {"id": "6c8947f3-3f5e-4887-ac0c-1c74422860bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image ethics and provenance", "children": [{"id": "4121fbe9-2a1d-463a-bbdb-671430f2b1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthetic images and disclosure"}, {"id": "c1259f7d-1736-4d90-b3bd-a34d7376eaf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata and content credentials"}, {"id": "ea43993d-1b25-447d-9bfb-979fd977b7e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias in image datasets"}, {"id": "326f3d73-f87a-4015-a3d6-cb824d5e2ca8", "type": "concept", "title": "Appropriation, consent, and fair use questions"}], "description": "Students examine manipulation as both artistic method and public trust problem."}]}, {"id": "980e8657-e361-4bd4-954a-28dcdfdd9b52", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Painting, Drawing, Collage, and Hybrid Image-Making", "description": "Digital painting is not just traditional drawing on a screen. This unit explores brushes, tablets, collage systems, procedural textures, and hybrid workflows that combine analog and digital marks.", "children": [{"id": "32c4734d-9f97-475d-b7cf-bee49e6de22a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital drawing tools and mark-making", "children": [{"id": "9e048ad5-bf77-4e00-99d4-62e223f9334b", "type": "concept", "title": "Tablet ergonomics and calibration"}, {"id": "216046df-5840-4191-8c9e-a674483bb9f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Brush design and texture"}, {"id": "d15a0bf3-00bb-4d01-8ef4-eca328c2cf77", "type": "concept", "title": "Line, value, gesture, and surface"}, {"id": "36627aa9-ed57-4239-ab74-aecfab48fd02", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow from sketch to finished image"}], "description": "Students learn how pressure, texture, brushes, layers, and stylus control shape expressive visual language."}, {"id": "62ad75f4-aa6a-4374-b10b-0c1eb0b159e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collage and mixed-media translation", "children": [{"id": "f8a18085-1af0-41b5-8d58-a04a7638b557", "type": "concept", "title": "Scanning and photographing source material"}, {"id": "9d46c1c5-08f5-430f-b081-eadc6b733211", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutout, collage, and assemblage methods"}, {"id": "ef2d3230-f892-4494-a814-9df40eecf2ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern, repetition, and sampling"}, {"id": "edbda028-8a67-47ff-9113-4b9d32fc7cce", "type": "concept", "title": "Analog texture in digital space"}], "description": "Students practice moving between paper, scanner, camera, tablet, and software."}, {"id": "8f58f0fe-4696-408f-9f99-caa4b901625f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image series and visual systems", "children": [{"id": "1274aa5a-0afa-47bb-b1c7-a7d065dd2d85", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation and constraint"}, {"id": "bcc8ae08-e827-4fb7-85dd-12336c39cfb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Style systems and visual identity"}, {"id": "49c4f066-11a9-40ae-9b2a-2c8b05e59340", "type": "concept", "title": "Print, screen, and installation presentation"}, {"id": "5c177da7-362c-4253-984d-336c6eed7878", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique of consistency and surprise"}], "description": "The unit encourages students to think in bodies of work rather than isolated images."}]}, {"id": "a50519db-6a93-4686-b1a2-6b36a1e5f8eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Time-Based Media: Video, Editing, Motion, and Animation", "description": "Time-based media teaches students to compose with duration, rhythm, sequence, and change. This unit bridges video art, motion graphics, animation, and experimental editing.", "children": [{"id": "1b39d27f-7745-41df-b8a1-5add39be79b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Video capture and editing language", "children": [{"id": "5b4d30e1-6a22-4dea-b9d9-09507e492d71", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot types and continuity"}, {"id": "04b17cf1-ab15-4362-9192-392aebc396d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Montage and associative editing"}, {"id": "77bd8231-f7a6-4d6f-883d-6daf260d7d48", "type": "concept", "title": "Color correction and grading basics"}, {"id": "597c9fb0-71d6-4eb1-8e3c-98d51bc6ede5", "type": "concept", "title": "Export settings for screen and projection"}], "description": "Students learn how framing, motion, sequence, pacing, and montage create meaning."}, {"id": "82867abf-41e6-404f-8819-65204d1e5f56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Animation and motion design", "children": [{"id": "e6b77ef0-9c0c-4bc8-971e-99973bf61454", "type": "concept", "title": "Frame-by-frame and keyframe animation"}, {"id": "944b2ec5-cf47-40c6-b349-7ad9b324f2ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Easing, timing, and rhythm"}, {"id": "476446ca-a2d9-4163-97d8-d08d749ffb99", "type": "concept", "title": "Loops, GIFs, and short-form motion"}, {"id": "078f8158-4bdc-4fd6-9ebd-b7321425b180", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography and moving image"}], "description": "Students build fluency in keyframes, timing, loops, and motion principles."}, {"id": "4fcb5308-333e-4beb-b57f-bb73d3fe2b0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experimental time-based forms", "children": [{"id": "d9c46925-96fa-4896-8756-721f4fa7d8a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-channel video"}, {"id": "5da3d5ed-1962-4d58-857d-f1c16c1a7e53", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-channel installation"}, {"id": "cee4f277-15d2-4598-9c28-2bacc4e83a55", "type": "concept", "title": "Live video and feedback"}, {"id": "fb53bcab-8d02-43b7-8a57-cba2d92014a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Found footage and remix"}], "description": "The aim is to understand video as installation, performance record, screen work, and networked media."}]}, {"id": "17f91233-ac58-4cc1-b8f9-5c1db0780109", "type": "topic", "title": "Sound Art, Audio Editing, Sampling, and Spatial Listening", "description": "Sound expands digital art beyond the visual. Students learn to listen, record, edit, spatialize, and integrate audio as material, environment, signal, and interface.", "children": [{"id": "0f685a1a-54cb-4a1c-bb31-b28a7d1ba47c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening and field recording", "children": [{"id": "1269d787-8fb3-45ad-b077-cb00ecc44b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Microphone types and placement"}, {"id": "477bcf49-6b2c-4dfe-8507-2468a2f0ae6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambient, voice, and object recording"}, {"id": "21337c89-7e47-496a-a1d5-6b8af8908592", "type": "concept", "title": "Noise floors and room tone"}, {"id": "94c7f2e4-6e3d-4435-b190-e36962d6cc6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Soundwalks and acoustic ecology"}], "description": "Students learn that sound work begins with attention: what is heard, where it is heard, and how recording transforms it."}, {"id": "e74c7f8a-e8c1-484d-84ee-837a95b4d327", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editing, sampling, and composition", "children": [{"id": "255a35c3-abab-4378-8688-b667e2175004", "type": "concept", "title": "Waveform editing"}, {"id": "6fca3d5f-044c-4ab4-a3eb-5989bc620433", "type": "concept", "title": "Layering, looping, and envelopes"}, {"id": "9da4e64b-225f-49a0-a992-154e084fcd19", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling ethics and copyright"}, {"id": "4e8f8817-1301-4bed-bd35-713630d4d2aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice, texture, rhythm, and silence"}], "description": "Students build short works from recorded, synthesized, and found sound."}, {"id": "21104ac8-7a9e-452a-ba63-f0c4eb5d75c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sound in installation and interaction", "children": [{"id": "f9d1927d-b5f1-44a0-9f95-b116480ccf72", "type": "concept", "title": "Speakers and spatial placement"}, {"id": "d4c0b6e0-ed5d-4123-a882-92151397420c", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive and generative sound"}, {"id": "87ce84b4-72d1-4f53-8948-afbf454e80cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio-reactive visuals"}, {"id": "477fb7b9-551a-4ce1-8b01-8dd093d023d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility and captioning"}], "description": "The unit connects audio to space, bodies, and systems."}]}, {"id": "79523e38-6197-48be-bf16-ceb13811ebca", "type": "topic", "title": "Creative Coding Foundations: Processing, p5.js, and Generative Systems", "description": "Creative coding lets students design processes rather than only fixed artifacts. This unit introduces programming as a studio material for drawing, animation, chance, interaction, and generative form.", "children": [{"id": "4689ddf3-ade2-4a18-bbc2-4b774043a388", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Programming fundamentals for artists", "children": [{"id": "245c18d1-afdd-43c6-984b-0446fbf78c53", "type": "concept", "title": "Variables, conditionals, loops, and functions"}, {"id": "0516d151-e542-4cab-bb04-7adaf1f58007", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordinate systems and transforms"}, {"id": "36218f6a-3bcd-4521-88ab-f9cc6f157a39", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, shape, and typography"}, {"id": "bb47360a-a1ae-42e6-8f1f-8099f22b3119", "type": "concept", "title": "Debugging and code reading"}], "description": "Students learn enough code to sketch visually, debug calmly, and treat computation as an expressive medium."}, {"id": "cdd0cbca-a343-4f96-ba73-7d014ab7d7fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Generative systems", "children": [{"id": "5f77f986-b162-4ea4-8da4-f87f54dab501", "type": "concept", "title": "Randomness and noise"}, {"id": "9f20addc-f496-4c65-93cc-95764d86013d", "type": "concept", "title": "Recursion and repetition"}, {"id": "3bb63662-69c4-460a-ac1d-5f38b3203a2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Particle systems and agents"}, {"id": "42c05414-201a-4e3b-a93e-4f4ad09b8afc", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraint-based composition"}], "description": "Students explore how rules, randomness, data, and feedback can produce visual complexity."}, {"id": "446fa4c3-ee50-4734-bef2-2982e4b026cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Publishing and sharing sketches", "children": [{"id": "dd930d87-b038-473e-882c-0e4a75b160da", "type": "concept", "title": "p5.js web sketches"}, {"id": "b537d218-9321-445e-ac09-04469b7f8671", "type": "concept", "title": "Processing exports"}, {"id": "5c5193b6-284d-4c22-994f-2756aaf84659", "type": "concept", "title": "Code comments and artist notes"}, {"id": "ea5f33c6-7bc3-4919-be51-2353d650d04a", "type": "concept", "title": "Open-source etiquette"}], "description": "The goal is to move code out of the classroom and into critique, portfolios, browsers, and installations."}]}, {"id": "457cc981-ff32-41e4-8509-423c2d67acf6", "type": "topic", "title": "Web-Based, Networked, and Browser-Based Art", "description": "The web is both a medium and a public site of distribution. This unit treats HTML, CSS, JavaScript, networks, browsers, and platforms as artistic materials.", "children": [{"id": "e26659dc-1d46-4441-ade6-f11382a9336a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for artists", "children": [{"id": "3d26b66c-fb83-45a8-8c13-f2017de1e82c", "type": "concept", "title": "Semantic HTML"}, {"id": "2eacc05e-2155-4697-8ae5-63574625f905", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive CSS and layout"}, {"id": "9b898725-971f-452a-b8d2-46764dbc5d05", "type": "concept", "title": "JavaScript events"}, {"id": "d9fd3720-f553-449c-9837-20aadc221b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Media, embeds, and browser APIs"}], "description": "Students learn enough web structure, style, and scripting to create authored browser experiences."}, {"id": "27764614-bf8a-4fd3-97a8-0d47d24de3d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Networked and participatory forms", "children": [{"id": "0c603000-da62-448c-a74a-8cc5975f7d54", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypertext and nonlinear navigation"}, {"id": "5543e4c8-0b4a-4b16-8c0a-02e718b3d59a", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media as site and material"}, {"id": "dd2a96de-9776-4aba-bb9a-10a767ea5342", "type": "concept", "title": "APIs and live data"}, {"id": "f57f38a0-5edb-4be1-98f8-e142aebd177d", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective authorship and moderation"}], "description": "Students examine artworks that depend on users, data flows, links, social systems, or distributed participation."}, {"id": "072c9c45-ed42-49be-b021-43234a745035", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Web accessibility and resilience", "children": [{"id": "58031cb7-9138-4095-bedd-78969bfb2fb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and keyboard access"}, {"id": "1e37bf34-d5e9-4777-a6a0-645e828a0270", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance and low-bandwidth design"}, {"id": "9b58a2c6-9e0f-4747-bf64-a0f73ad5012d", "type": "concept", "title": "Progressive enhancement"}, {"id": "2fc98382-c213-4857-bc48-102372df8877", "type": "concept", "title": "Domain, hosting, and link rot"}], "description": "The point is to make browser works more usable, ethical, and durable."}]}, {"id": "dc33ff42-1dfe-46ae-9b53-cbc38a6ee2e7", "type": "topic", "title": "Interactivity: Sensors, Microcontrollers, Physical Computing, and Participation", "description": "Interactive art joins software to bodies, spaces, objects, and behavior. This unit introduces physical computing and participatory design as ways to make systems that sense and respond.", "children": [{"id": "b6c1b3f2-b4a6-4add-871b-3665006b6dd9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interaction design for artworks", "children": [{"id": "55b8a3a9-e952-44e6-b48c-364b008de92e", "type": "concept", "title": "Affordances and feedback"}, {"id": "04c7bf03-9340-456a-9c43-99b1ed13da15", "type": "concept", "title": "Input, output, state, and response"}, {"id": "c5b538e2-136d-47e3-bdca-fadb9a3ff8b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Instructions and audience behavior"}, {"id": "1e7120db-c8fd-46b5-9c5c-d089502da517", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure modes and graceful recovery"}], "description": "Students learn how to design encounters, not just mechanisms."}, {"id": "b5b8a1c9-574f-4ea1-96d7-28e98113c8b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensors and microcontrollers", "children": [{"id": "f8406ff2-f9fe-4fab-816f-08f7a178374d", "type": "concept", "title": "Arduino boards and circuits"}, {"id": "370bc16f-3f82-4b5b-818b-98413c2be5e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Buttons, knobs, light, distance, and motion sensors"}, {"id": "8d67ce4e-79da-418f-aedf-5446052090de", "type": "concept", "title": "LEDs, motors, and displays"}, {"id": "e307a32d-1542-44b9-85aa-746b9ad8cc86", "type": "concept", "title": "Serial communication"}], "description": "Students prototype simple responsive systems using physical inputs and outputs."}, {"id": "49c1b226-2a5d-4cc2-8df8-83d1950bc1a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participation, consent, and care", "children": [{"id": "3a93e904-62a5-47cc-bbd0-3a57465a4ad7", "type": "concept", "title": "Data capture and consent"}, {"id": "e43bb7c8-7aca-4c23-af89-d799e6860603", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible interaction"}, {"id": "a3d52873-5a1f-45af-ab45-755a6349c27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Public versus private participation"}, {"id": "eb2898ff-9607-4001-9c6d-444c0870e774", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance during exhibition"}], "description": "Students consider how interactive systems affect bodies, privacy, agency, and access."}]}, {"id": "455e08a5-2231-4baa-b657-34965110cf64", "type": "topic", "title": "3D Modeling, Rendering, Simulation, and Virtual Space", "description": "Three-dimensional digital work gives students tools for sculpture, environment, image-making, animation, fabrication, and immersive worlds. This unit teaches 3D thinking without reducing it to software buttons.", "children": [{"id": "f0cc49c9-a314-4735-a4a1-c3fab3847d7c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modeling and scene construction", "children": [{"id": "5feb43b0-07f4-47f3-9b82-c6604677cc57", "type": "concept", "title": "Mesh, curve, and primitive modeling"}, {"id": "c7e96f04-eb3a-45d2-a180-4ded815d0938", "type": "concept", "title": "Topology and normals"}, {"id": "1ddf20d0-de4b-44ea-a9a8-c779ae43d19e", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale and units"}, {"id": "1462462a-16af-4786-972a-5ecaeca3dc6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene organization"}], "description": "Students learn how objects, surfaces, scale, and spatial relationships are built in digital environments."}, {"id": "b9478fb6-6677-4824-83c8-841ea52fe3b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materials, lighting, and rendering", "children": [{"id": "81d4ca59-2fa2-49c5-ab64-ca066a00c562", "type": "concept", "title": "Shaders and materials"}, {"id": "305e2742-ab48-4529-85df-edb5fa6fa586", "type": "concept", "title": "UVs and procedural textures"}, {"id": "35017a7b-aabd-46a4-932e-ad1461e7403d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting setups"}, {"id": "5ec427f5-6d1c-40ef-b5f5-b41b6dfd233e", "type": "concept", "title": "Still and animated renders"}], "description": "Students study how light, surface, texture, and camera settings create atmosphere and meaning."}, {"id": "4d3bde48-0953-420a-9b19-75627e119258", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simulation and virtual sculpture", "children": [{"id": "26724917-365a-4351-af72-497b5359ba07", "type": "concept", "title": "Physics simulation"}, {"id": "a039dc9a-72dd-4c99-8ceb-82f4ffd15f7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Particles and fields"}, {"id": "8e14f434-4cb1-4a26-b934-0f7d9e51f0a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural landscapes"}, {"id": "484137df-d682-4864-aa1a-28da471e8ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Export for web, game engines, or fabrication"}], "description": "The unit introduces systems that behave over time, from cloth and particles to procedural environments."}]}, {"id": "67e8e0ca-2400-48b0-80c5-a0cc2dd86f6c", "type": "topic", "title": "Game Engines, Real-Time Environments, AR/VR/XR, and Immersive Media", "description": "Real-time media changes the artwork from a fixed output into a responsive world. Students learn how game engines and immersive platforms support spatial storytelling, simulation, performance, and installation.", "children": [{"id": "391d860e-a4f1-4cac-89a4-b614f815272b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Game engine fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "f2219d06-dfbc-4758-9645-c5ff742c046c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenes, assets, and prefabs"}, {"id": "1f1e8ecf-9109-4c98-97c9-e4d662189c17", "type": "concept", "title": "Cameras, lights, and materials"}, {"id": "7237bf1b-35f0-4116-bc1c-6dc18875d081", "type": "concept", "title": "Physics and collision"}, {"id": "81756c53-83d8-4b4a-af39-7616e069b81d", "type": "concept", "title": "Build settings and deployment"}], "description": "Students learn core concepts that transfer across Unity, Unreal, and similar real-time tools."}, {"id": "f816e4c7-edc4-4458-85ce-d439e1261a4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Worldbuilding and interactive experience", "children": [{"id": "f3293314-f818-4204-af02-f107f6a38638", "type": "concept", "title": "Level and environment design"}, {"id": "fa48154c-d4a2-4738-ac4c-b6d9a5557e5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Navigation and player perspective"}, {"id": "e2505560-d88b-4bf2-a893-d91f8c193c5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound and spatial cues"}, {"id": "40c0f474-d6bc-4e5d-9074-21b0f4ea9942", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules, goals, and ambiguity"}], "description": "Students design navigable spaces with mood, pacing, agency, and constraints."}, {"id": "df61fa2f-e8bf-49ae-bddd-954a457288da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AR, VR, XR, and ethics of immersion", "children": [{"id": "9d49ef7b-2a81-490f-ac1b-a57a185e2543", "type": "concept", "title": "Headsets and mobile AR"}, {"id": "90f3c7c9-e93c-4080-a0a1-ba1754da496e", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion comfort and embodiment"}, {"id": "9d3a9e37-dd4a-48df-8e24-403520878ee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial UI"}, {"id": "c5568874-8b91-493e-a598-ed4e73eab51b", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, surveillance, and presence"}], "description": "The unit frames immersive media as embodied experience with technical, social, and accessibility stakes."}]}, {"id": "7d6a4c81-4cc0-4406-ae03-754b5aa89163", "type": "topic", "title": "Data, Visualization, Machine Vision, AI, and Algorithmic Critique", "description": "Artists increasingly work with datasets, models, sensors, and automated systems. This unit teaches students to use algorithmic tools while questioning what they measure, omit, classify, and amplify.", "children": [{"id": "115e3476-2d00-40cf-8c63-21484fb5687b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data as artistic material", "children": [{"id": "2685cdf4-eca3-42f3-b185-7ebf4370193e", "type": "concept", "title": "Dataset sources and documentation"}, {"id": "9924efc4-b54a-42d6-8c89-bcc0a12042ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleaning and uncertainty"}, {"id": "2e703ec0-9730-45f7-8915-97cfd7e3559d", "type": "concept", "title": "Mappings from data to image, sound, or motion"}, {"id": "ef79ae23-e5f5-49df-bd37-90fe93d96f4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data feminism and situated knowledge"}], "description": "Students learn to gather, clean, interpret, and transform data into form without pretending data is neutral."}, {"id": "28e1bb0c-e49c-4657-91db-a343775b2273", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Machine vision and AI systems", "children": [{"id": "b584e9c4-9d6d-405e-8c2b-a3d4ea8e9bc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Image classification and detection"}, {"id": "e909ffef-8f98-425e-890c-9265ddc3f3a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Pose and face tracking"}, {"id": "f57acfc8-ff17-460b-83b4-e8aa41b419e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Text-to-image and generative tools"}, {"id": "9d34ae87-2980-417f-a492-70daeb916513", "type": "concept", "title": "Model limits, bias, and hallucination"}], "description": "Students explore computer vision and AI-assisted making as creative tools and cultural objects."}, {"id": "93035d91-2d3e-465b-9e8d-7c3f61abc235", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Algorithmic critique", "children": [{"id": "7e4e362c-6416-4797-ba0c-6def75608e04", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias and representational harm"}, {"id": "112aa7ad-cf77-491b-9211-35b14f77d22d", "type": "concept", "title": "Training data and consent"}, {"id": "ad141116-29a9-4ec0-8541-e8c21fe188ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation and labor"}, {"id": "6aafc408-67f6-48e7-a50b-cf55db182b64", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency, refusal, and counter-design"}], "description": "The goal is to understand computation as power: classification, prediction, sorting, and automation."}]}, {"id": "c6d1449a-e2af-464f-93c0-6ac35133800f", "type": "topic", "title": "Installation, Projection Mapping, Exhibition Design, and Technical Production", "description": "New media works often become real only in space. This unit teaches students to design for walls, rooms, bodies, light, sound, cables, projectors, screens, and gallery operations.", "children": [{"id": "91c1ed5c-5c05-4da3-a974-02f4c12b2358", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition planning and spatial design", "children": [{"id": "99f8cc7d-6b03-4d3d-a9f2-e9a4bf0703a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and sightlines"}, {"id": "b406ca03-b76e-4435-bb50-8004db62ca3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Screens, projectors, speakers, and mounts"}, {"id": "e3baadba-1ad4-46d8-9716-bb0f79ac9a3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience flow and dwell time"}, {"id": "ee0305eb-fe1b-49bd-a322-f07265be789c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and environmental constraints"}], "description": "Students learn to translate a digital idea into a physical encounter."}, {"id": "18f69e1b-b7ba-480b-a4df-c96ae879f7ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Projection mapping and live media systems", "children": [{"id": "cb137c94-a9fe-4b9a-873d-17a324543d76", "type": "concept", "title": "Projector placement and keystone"}, {"id": "fdf006dd-0c2e-41de-8648-b31cac11a9df", "type": "concept", "title": "Masks and mapping surfaces"}, {"id": "7ce5be09-bc37-4b03-9b62-8a327e64a04d", "type": "concept", "title": "TouchDesigner and real-time routing"}, {"id": "49d369af-3677-4d45-bdf6-d467658c25d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Latency and synchronization"}], "description": "Students explore how images can be aligned to architecture, objects, and performance."}, {"id": "1c422c48-f2f3-420e-92c4-6c750919f04c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Technical production and troubleshooting", "children": [{"id": "4b22cc3a-0d28-40c1-a765-c0d9c3242226", "type": "concept", "title": "Equipment lists and signal flow"}, {"id": "ca0d7b6b-091f-43b7-bdef-17cd87d47e05", "type": "concept", "title": "Cable management and labeling"}, {"id": "55c0c274-3ecd-4591-b572-8f771500ad0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Startup and shutdown procedures"}, {"id": "566dccf5-0869-4601-bdda-e47167976416", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment and backups"}], "description": "The unit builds practical readiness for installing, testing, maintaining, and deinstalling work."}]}, {"id": "5a4b680b-74d4-4375-83cf-32424bbf6770", "type": "topic", "title": "Preservation, Documentation, Accessibility, Copyright, and Platform Ethics", "description": "Digital artworks are fragile because platforms, formats, hardware, and social contexts change. This unit teaches students to document, license, preserve, and present work responsibly.", "children": [{"id": "485c79f9-b53c-4d00-a32a-67e586a586d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation and preservation strategies", "children": [{"id": "d748b81e-c953-4c94-aa40-36451cc1ab0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Screenshots, video walkthroughs, and source files"}, {"id": "d48ee3f1-a9ab-47d6-8c3e-d1a018940800", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist interviews and installation manuals"}, {"id": "434142ac-944e-47d2-9059-df76a477ed5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration, emulation, and reinterpretation"}, {"id": "5c49b290-5d25-4d2a-b990-6f422f314aac", "type": "concept", "title": "Dependency and version documentation"}], "description": "Students learn to create records that help future viewers, curators, collaborators, and the artist's own archive."}, {"id": "b9047626-d627-43aa-ae2b-72f3709acc6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and inclusive presentation", "children": [{"id": "d0aad3c2-4f03-491a-9195-29c7954868e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Captions and transcripts"}, {"id": "44fdabf3-dc6e-4a41-9894-2b4fc09dbf1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and audio description"}, {"id": "04a4b5a1-4352-45c2-8d93-68c52dd2f08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyboard and assistive technology support"}, {"id": "52701d46-eda4-4916-b8c5-c5867161de1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensory and mobility considerations"}], "description": "The goal is to treat access as part of the artwork's design, not an afterthought."}, {"id": "5acbe57c-01f6-42ba-acb5-65706f1ed0b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Copyright, licensing, and platform ethics", "children": [{"id": "a598ba6c-0f86-4c8a-9d76-516ad5df0092", "type": "concept", "title": "Fair use and appropriation"}, {"id": "79ea13bb-00c1-4843-9c77-c2f42282cc56", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative Commons licenses"}, {"id": "41371366-3ff2-4f5d-a11a-14f2d37c2c0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Terms of service and platform dependency"}, {"id": "a06b4fbf-82fc-42c9-af2a-342f55d0faf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, and community standards"}], "description": "Students learn how to use, remix, publish, and protect work with legal and ethical literacy."}]}, {"id": "ac0fe405-7143-4b81-8bdd-ddd44188d5c0", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone New Media Studio: Prototype, Iterate, Critique, Exhibit, and Reflect", "description": "The capstone brings the course together through an ambitious, self-directed project. Students move from proposal to prototype to public presentation, supported by critique, documentation, and reflective writing.", "children": [{"id": "92e10c2a-85c0-4b36-91d8-ba5756be13fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project proposal and research", "children": [{"id": "011b8225-ab83-433b-a1ca-09c97be0aaec", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept statement"}, {"id": "28b02c7c-b45f-414c-b0f4-569114deb76f", "type": "concept", "title": "Research precedents"}, {"id": "42144f1c-0b40-4d3e-be0a-08ddefe71844", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical feasibility"}, {"id": "9b2cefdb-22a5-456d-ab74-318feb483975", "type": "concept", "title": "Schedule and materials budget"}], "description": "Students define an artistic question, audience, technical approach, references, and production plan."}, {"id": "d3179c77-fde2-4dab-b282-4528bbcc52eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype and iteration cycle", "children": [{"id": "0ee62cf3-c05a-4cbc-9f1e-f9d232c75c1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-fidelity prototypes"}, {"id": "eb408496-bf9d-42f6-afa9-9d7812054cd2", "type": "concept", "title": "User or viewer testing"}, {"id": "486d8b3d-33ae-44aa-8518-6b39782b20ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique-based revision"}, {"id": "87ea344d-d4fe-49cf-afe3-c38e1433c2bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical problem logs"}], "description": "Students learn to test quickly, critique honestly, and revise based on evidence."}, {"id": "7626369b-9477-42e1-a24a-0e2401a1d02a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition and reflective practice", "children": [{"id": "622fb6f6-dab1-4389-9d96-f9cde07cf471", "type": "concept", "title": "Installation plan"}, {"id": "fdcef5a8-f673-4557-96f0-88f3295fa816", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statement"}, {"id": "b714e69e-1d99-4b3c-8641-55adb077a42b", "type": "concept", "title": "Process archive"}, {"id": "2344cf30-14dd-4614-a3df-ca8f29c3d204", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio-ready documentation"}], "description": "The final work is presented with documentation that explains choices, context, and future development."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$digajson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'digital-art-new-media'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Digital Art / New Media',
  goal = 'Digital Art / New Media',
  summary = 'Digital Art / New Media is an advanced studio course in contemporary art practices that use digital tools, code, networks, time-based media, sensors, real-time systems, data, AI, and installation technologies. Students learn to make images, moving works, sound pieces, web-based artworks, generative sketches, interactive prototypes, 3D environments, and exhibition-ready projects while developing historical awareness, critique fluency, ethical judgment, technical resilience, and documentation practices.',
  data = $digajson${"slug": "digital-art-new-media", "title": "Digital Art / New Media", "description": "Digital Art / New Media is an advanced studio course in contemporary art practices that use digital tools, code, networks, time-based media, sensors, real-time systems, data, AI, and installation technologies. Students learn to make images, moving works, sound pieces, web-based artworks, generative sketches, interactive prototypes, 3D environments, and exhibition-ready projects while developing historical awareness, critique fluency, ethical judgment, technical resilience, and documentation practices.", "topics": [{"id": "5c2494d0-035f-4b31-b1d3-09a4b3eff2c3", "type": "topic", "title": "New Media Art Histories, Concepts, and Studio Critique", "description": "This opening unit gives students a shared language for understanding digital art as an artistic, cultural, and technological practice. It connects studio making to histories of video art, net art, systems art, cyberfeminism, tactical media, interactive installation, and contemporary platform culture.", "children": [{"id": "59c3974f-fc9c-4af7-9c6e-b56455d8f11f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital and new media art lineages", "children": [{"id": "5b360352-d422-49a8-b1b9-2a14a9df9c0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Video art and expanded cinema"}, {"id": "af0af1d2-8d6b-43ac-a9aa-972ffa032924", "type": "concept", "title": "Net.art and browser-based work"}, {"id": "53b4bf30-46ea-4562-8988-8a567ffa44d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybernetic, systems, and generative traditions"}, {"id": "97a06fb0-3ff9-4dce-8eb5-92f3441c6d59", "type": "concept", "title": "Institutional critique and tactical media"}], "description": "Students learn how digital practice grows from earlier experiments in photography, video, conceptual art, performance, systems aesthetics, and computer graphics."}, {"id": "be96edd4-9253-4f60-a4d0-a7dfbbd7c3b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Critical vocabulary for technology and culture", "children": [{"id": "1c4c6eec-5458-4992-b81b-732431466656", "type": "concept", "title": "Interface, database, network, protocol, platform"}, {"id": "61614c5c-2719-4592-bc45-a23f2673874c", "type": "concept", "title": "Simulation, interactivity, immersion, remediation"}, {"id": "0ac1375d-d4c7-4dee-8336-a43abc74f45d", "type": "concept", "title": "Post-internet and platform aesthetics"}, {"id": "56bea24d-70a5-4a05-a3d3-c27ebc65541b", "type": "concept", "title": "Attention, surveillance, labor, and identity"}], "description": "The point is to move beyond tool fluency and ask what digital systems do socially, politically, and aesthetically."}, {"id": "5322a723-2c64-40dc-81e7-73610e07fcbd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Studio critique methods", "children": [{"id": "11cd3ff1-e5fc-40aa-8aba-5da393a93879", "type": "concept", "title": "Description, analysis, interpretation, judgment"}, {"id": "dd8ce1a1-debb-43d2-b834-b73c69372655", "type": "concept", "title": "Prototype critique versus finished-work critique"}, {"id": "2c78e46c-8b97-4a6c-bba3-21f1024d8b3a", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statements and process documentation"}, {"id": "83d658c6-493a-4f2b-9f0c-0e2c6f240c11", "type": "concept", "title": "Respectful, evidence-based feedback"}], "description": "Students practice giving and receiving critique that addresses concept, form, experience, craft, accessibility, and technical implementation."}]}, {"id": "9fe36c43-e21f-45fc-81d3-33e2ba50f7e6", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Workflow, File Formats, Color, Resolution, and Archiving", "description": "This unit builds the durable habits that let artists move work across software, screens, projectors, printers, web platforms, and archives without losing quality or meaning.", "children": [{"id": "4867e580-d57a-47c5-97f0-8bb404494f52", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital workflow and versioning", "children": [{"id": "ef305c1a-0ce0-4f8c-994a-99fd90deeb36", "type": "concept", "title": "Folder structures and naming conventions"}, {"id": "32616e28-279a-41c9-8980-794dc26bba73", "type": "concept", "title": "Source files versus exports"}, {"id": "17e15002-6720-429f-83c6-3b77ac442f45", "type": "concept", "title": "Version notes and iteration logs"}, {"id": "daa7065e-6fb6-4917-adbc-a6a55cfc0379", "type": "concept", "title": "Backup rules and cloud/local redundancy"}], "description": "Students learn to organize projects so experiments remain reversible, inspectable, and shareable."}, {"id": "38251d44-0299-4345-b03a-8e5cc2c8a3fc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resolution, compression, and formats", "children": [{"id": "5b0be1a2-254d-47af-8dd6-1262357c015e", "type": "concept", "title": "Raster and vector files"}, {"id": "59527d82-618f-4ab9-bcdc-8b8e2cb326ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Lossless and lossy compression"}, {"id": "e887b0c3-3a33-472e-b7a6-5a6f8625a043", "type": "concept", "title": "Web, print, projection, and installation exports"}, {"id": "49e159db-6e3b-485a-9715-2913b15e2242", "type": "concept", "title": "Code repositories and packaged projects"}], "description": "The gist is knowing what a file is, what it preserves, and what it throws away."}, {"id": "111ee271-5cfc-4bcc-ac3a-91307a5a87fb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Color and display management", "children": [{"id": "6717820e-ed13-414f-b630-aaa8bde815ce", "type": "concept", "title": "RGB, CMYK, indexed color, and alpha"}, {"id": "c67d039a-199e-40fe-bb9b-c8925e167355", "type": "concept", "title": "Color profiles and calibration"}, {"id": "694dbf7e-5158-48cd-986a-b3477d032bf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Bit depth and dynamic range"}, {"id": "c1705345-3718-41ff-9a14-ba24cdf6d006", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility and contrast"}], "description": "Students develop practical judgment about how color changes across monitors, projectors, print, and mobile devices."}]}, {"id": "e2db2161-c493-4f34-918b-943e250c84d2", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Imaging, Compositing, and Photographic Manipulation", "description": "This unit treats the digital image as a constructed object. Students learn how to manipulate, composite, repair, distort, and question photographic images while staying alert to ethics and visual evidence.", "children": [{"id": "dd1a4839-89bc-4816-be8b-7a98c8765d62", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Layer-based image construction", "children": [{"id": "827b51eb-1ed5-4c58-a458-38b4a60b05b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Selections and masking"}, {"id": "34f78fae-f8c9-4e7b-ad77-541a9ed015fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Adjustment layers and blending modes"}, {"id": "b1bbfff4-dda8-4124-98a9-c3d2b39e84e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Smart objects and non-destructive edits"}, {"id": "02a8d968-fb13-4737-b71b-8f61e9911301", "type": "concept", "title": "Image cleanup and repair"}], "description": "Students learn how complex images are built through non-destructive layering, masks, selections, and adjustment systems."}, {"id": "6234a6f3-ccd7-46b7-ac1c-e44166217fcc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compositing and montage", "children": [{"id": "aa2a659c-e6cb-4160-9ac3-efcfc253b878", "type": "concept", "title": "Perspective matching"}, {"id": "64c3f9c3-72ad-474b-9b95-8c3e55a4051e", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and shadow logic"}, {"id": "777f2162-e19a-40c7-b237-5dac1ce872ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Texture and grain consistency"}, {"id": "e39de29a-662d-4a0d-b114-581e9713c063", "type": "concept", "title": "Surreal, documentary, and speculative montage"}], "description": "The goal is to build convincing or deliberately unstable visual worlds through scale, light, color, and perspective."}, {"id": "6c8947f3-3f5e-4887-ac0c-1c74422860bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image ethics and provenance", "children": [{"id": "4121fbe9-2a1d-463a-bbdb-671430f2b1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Synthetic images and disclosure"}, {"id": "c1259f7d-1736-4d90-b3bd-a34d7376eaf7", "type": "concept", "title": "Metadata and content credentials"}, {"id": "ea43993d-1b25-447d-9bfb-979fd977b7e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias in image datasets"}, {"id": "326f3d73-f87a-4015-a3d6-cb824d5e2ca8", "type": "concept", "title": "Appropriation, consent, and fair use questions"}], "description": "Students examine manipulation as both artistic method and public trust problem."}]}, {"id": "980e8657-e361-4bd4-954a-28dcdfdd9b52", "type": "topic", "title": "Digital Painting, Drawing, Collage, and Hybrid Image-Making", "description": "Digital painting is not just traditional drawing on a screen. This unit explores brushes, tablets, collage systems, procedural textures, and hybrid workflows that combine analog and digital marks.", "children": [{"id": "32c4734d-9f97-475d-b7cf-bee49e6de22a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital drawing tools and mark-making", "children": [{"id": "9e048ad5-bf77-4e00-99d4-62e223f9334b", "type": "concept", "title": "Tablet ergonomics and calibration"}, {"id": "216046df-5840-4191-8c9e-a674483bb9f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Brush design and texture"}, {"id": "d15a0bf3-00bb-4d01-8ef4-eca328c2cf77", "type": "concept", "title": "Line, value, gesture, and surface"}, {"id": "36627aa9-ed57-4239-ab74-aecfab48fd02", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow from sketch to finished image"}], "description": "Students learn how pressure, texture, brushes, layers, and stylus control shape expressive visual language."}, {"id": "62ad75f4-aa6a-4374-b10b-0c1eb0b159e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Collage and mixed-media translation", "children": [{"id": "f8a18085-1af0-41b5-8d58-a04a7638b557", "type": "concept", "title": "Scanning and photographing source material"}, {"id": "9d46c1c5-08f5-430f-b081-eadc6b733211", "type": "concept", "title": "Cutout, collage, and assemblage methods"}, {"id": "ef2d3230-f892-4494-a814-9df40eecf2ef", "type": "concept", "title": "Pattern, repetition, and sampling"}, {"id": "edbda028-8a67-47ff-9113-4b9d32fc7cce", "type": "concept", "title": "Analog texture in digital space"}], "description": "Students practice moving between paper, scanner, camera, tablet, and software."}, {"id": "8f58f0fe-4696-408f-9f99-caa4b901625f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Image series and visual systems", "children": [{"id": "1274aa5a-0afa-47bb-b1c7-a7d065dd2d85", "type": "concept", "title": "Variation and constraint"}, {"id": "bcc8ae08-e827-4fb7-85dd-12336c39cfb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Style systems and visual identity"}, {"id": "49c4f066-11a9-40ae-9b2a-2c8b05e59340", "type": "concept", "title": "Print, screen, and installation presentation"}, {"id": "5c177da7-362c-4253-984d-336c6eed7878", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique of consistency and surprise"}], "description": "The unit encourages students to think in bodies of work rather than isolated images."}]}, {"id": "a50519db-6a93-4686-b1a2-6b36a1e5f8eb", "type": "topic", "title": "Time-Based Media: Video, Editing, Motion, and Animation", "description": "Time-based media teaches students to compose with duration, rhythm, sequence, and change. This unit bridges video art, motion graphics, animation, and experimental editing.", "children": [{"id": "1b39d27f-7745-41df-b8a1-5add39be79b1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Video capture and editing language", "children": [{"id": "5b4d30e1-6a22-4dea-b9d9-09507e492d71", "type": "concept", "title": "Shot types and continuity"}, {"id": "04b17cf1-ab15-4362-9192-392aebc396d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Montage and associative editing"}, {"id": "77bd8231-f7a6-4d6f-883d-6daf260d7d48", "type": "concept", "title": "Color correction and grading basics"}, {"id": "597c9fb0-71d6-4eb1-8e3c-98d51bc6ede5", "type": "concept", "title": "Export settings for screen and projection"}], "description": "Students learn how framing, motion, sequence, pacing, and montage create meaning."}, {"id": "82867abf-41e6-404f-8819-65204d1e5f56", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Animation and motion design", "children": [{"id": "e6b77ef0-9c0c-4bc8-971e-99973bf61454", "type": "concept", "title": "Frame-by-frame and keyframe animation"}, {"id": "944b2ec5-cf47-40c6-b349-7ad9b324f2ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Easing, timing, and rhythm"}, {"id": "476446ca-a2d9-4163-97d8-d08d749ffb99", "type": "concept", "title": "Loops, GIFs, and short-form motion"}, {"id": "078f8158-4bdc-4fd6-9ebd-b7321425b180", "type": "concept", "title": "Typography and moving image"}], "description": "Students build fluency in keyframes, timing, loops, and motion principles."}, {"id": "4fcb5308-333e-4beb-b57f-bb73d3fe2b0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Experimental time-based forms", "children": [{"id": "d9c46925-96fa-4896-8756-721f4fa7d8a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-channel video"}, {"id": "5da3d5ed-1962-4d58-857d-f1c16c1a7e53", "type": "concept", "title": "Multi-channel installation"}, {"id": "cee4f277-15d2-4598-9c28-2bacc4e83a55", "type": "concept", "title": "Live video and feedback"}, {"id": "fb53bcab-8d02-43b7-8a57-cba2d92014a3", "type": "concept", "title": "Found footage and remix"}], "description": "The aim is to understand video as installation, performance record, screen work, and networked media."}]}, {"id": "17f91233-ac58-4cc1-b8f9-5c1db0780109", "type": "topic", "title": "Sound Art, Audio Editing, Sampling, and Spatial Listening", "description": "Sound expands digital art beyond the visual. Students learn to listen, record, edit, spatialize, and integrate audio as material, environment, signal, and interface.", "children": [{"id": "0f685a1a-54cb-4a1c-bb31-b28a7d1ba47c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening and field recording", "children": [{"id": "1269d787-8fb3-45ad-b077-cb00ecc44b79", "type": "concept", "title": "Microphone types and placement"}, {"id": "477bcf49-6b2c-4dfe-8507-2468a2f0ae6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambient, voice, and object recording"}, {"id": "21337c89-7e47-496a-a1d5-6b8af8908592", "type": "concept", "title": "Noise floors and room tone"}, {"id": "94c7f2e4-6e3d-4435-b190-e36962d6cc6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Soundwalks and acoustic ecology"}], "description": "Students learn that sound work begins with attention: what is heard, where it is heard, and how recording transforms it."}, {"id": "e74c7f8a-e8c1-484d-84ee-837a95b4d327", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Editing, sampling, and composition", "children": [{"id": "255a35c3-abab-4378-8688-b667e2175004", "type": "concept", "title": "Waveform editing"}, {"id": "6fca3d5f-044c-4ab4-a3eb-5989bc620433", "type": "concept", "title": "Layering, looping, and envelopes"}, {"id": "9da4e64b-225f-49a0-a992-154e084fcd19", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling ethics and copyright"}, {"id": "4e8f8817-1301-4bed-bd35-713630d4d2aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice, texture, rhythm, and silence"}], "description": "Students build short works from recorded, synthesized, and found sound."}, {"id": "21104ac8-7a9e-452a-ba63-f0c4eb5d75c5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sound in installation and interaction", "children": [{"id": "f9d1927d-b5f1-44a0-9f95-b116480ccf72", "type": "concept", "title": "Speakers and spatial placement"}, {"id": "d4c0b6e0-ed5d-4123-a882-92151397420c", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive and generative sound"}, {"id": "87ce84b4-72d1-4f53-8948-afbf454e80cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Audio-reactive visuals"}, {"id": "477fb7b9-551a-4ce1-8b01-8dd093d023d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessibility and captioning"}], "description": "The unit connects audio to space, bodies, and systems."}]}, {"id": "79523e38-6197-48be-bf16-ceb13811ebca", "type": "topic", "title": "Creative Coding Foundations: Processing, p5.js, and Generative Systems", "description": "Creative coding lets students design processes rather than only fixed artifacts. This unit introduces programming as a studio material for drawing, animation, chance, interaction, and generative form.", "children": [{"id": "4689ddf3-ade2-4a18-bbc2-4b774043a388", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Programming fundamentals for artists", "children": [{"id": "245c18d1-afdd-43c6-984b-0446fbf78c53", "type": "concept", "title": "Variables, conditionals, loops, and functions"}, {"id": "0516d151-e542-4cab-bb04-7adaf1f58007", "type": "concept", "title": "Coordinate systems and transforms"}, {"id": "36218f6a-3bcd-4521-88ab-f9cc6f157a39", "type": "concept", "title": "Color, shape, and typography"}, {"id": "bb47360a-a1ae-42e6-8f1f-8099f22b3119", "type": "concept", "title": "Debugging and code reading"}], "description": "Students learn enough code to sketch visually, debug calmly, and treat computation as an expressive medium."}, {"id": "cdd0cbca-a343-4f96-ba73-7d014ab7d7fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Generative systems", "children": [{"id": "5f77f986-b162-4ea4-8da4-f87f54dab501", "type": "concept", "title": "Randomness and noise"}, {"id": "9f20addc-f496-4c65-93cc-95764d86013d", "type": "concept", "title": "Recursion and repetition"}, {"id": "3bb63662-69c4-460a-ac1d-5f38b3203a2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Particle systems and agents"}, {"id": "42c05414-201a-4e3b-a93e-4f4ad09b8afc", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraint-based composition"}], "description": "Students explore how rules, randomness, data, and feedback can produce visual complexity."}, {"id": "446fa4c3-ee50-4734-bef2-2982e4b026cb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Publishing and sharing sketches", "children": [{"id": "dd930d87-b038-473e-882c-0e4a75b160da", "type": "concept", "title": "p5.js web sketches"}, {"id": "b537d218-9321-445e-ac09-04469b7f8671", "type": "concept", "title": "Processing exports"}, {"id": "5c5193b6-284d-4c22-994f-2756aaf84659", "type": "concept", "title": "Code comments and artist notes"}, {"id": "ea5f33c6-7bc3-4919-be51-2353d650d04a", "type": "concept", "title": "Open-source etiquette"}], "description": "The goal is to move code out of the classroom and into critique, portfolios, browsers, and installations."}]}, {"id": "457cc981-ff32-41e4-8509-423c2d67acf6", "type": "topic", "title": "Web-Based, Networked, and Browser-Based Art", "description": "The web is both a medium and a public site of distribution. This unit treats HTML, CSS, JavaScript, networks, browsers, and platforms as artistic materials.", "children": [{"id": "e26659dc-1d46-4441-ade6-f11382a9336a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for artists", "children": [{"id": "3d26b66c-fb83-45a8-8c13-f2017de1e82c", "type": "concept", "title": "Semantic HTML"}, {"id": "2eacc05e-2155-4697-8ae5-63574625f905", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsive CSS and layout"}, {"id": "9b898725-971f-452a-b8d2-46764dbc5d05", "type": "concept", "title": "JavaScript events"}, {"id": "d9fd3720-f553-449c-9837-20aadc221b27", "type": "concept", "title": "Media, embeds, and browser APIs"}], "description": "Students learn enough web structure, style, and scripting to create authored browser experiences."}, {"id": "27764614-bf8a-4fd3-97a8-0d47d24de3d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Networked and participatory forms", "children": [{"id": "0c603000-da62-448c-a74a-8cc5975f7d54", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypertext and nonlinear navigation"}, {"id": "5543e4c8-0b4a-4b16-8c0a-02e718b3d59a", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media as site and material"}, {"id": "dd2a96de-9776-4aba-bb9a-10a767ea5342", "type": "concept", "title": "APIs and live data"}, {"id": "f57f38a0-5edb-4be1-98f8-e142aebd177d", "type": "concept", "title": "Collective authorship and moderation"}], "description": "Students examine artworks that depend on users, data flows, links, social systems, or distributed participation."}, {"id": "072c9c45-ed42-49be-b021-43234a745035", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Web accessibility and resilience", "children": [{"id": "58031cb7-9138-4095-bedd-78969bfb2fb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and keyboard access"}, {"id": "1e37bf34-d5e9-4777-a6a0-645e828a0270", "type": "concept", "title": "Performance and low-bandwidth design"}, {"id": "9b58a2c6-9e0f-4747-bf64-a0f73ad5012d", "type": "concept", "title": "Progressive enhancement"}, {"id": "2fc98382-c213-4857-bc48-102372df8877", "type": "concept", "title": "Domain, hosting, and link rot"}], "description": "The point is to make browser works more usable, ethical, and durable."}]}, {"id": "dc33ff42-1dfe-46ae-9b53-cbc38a6ee2e7", "type": "topic", "title": "Interactivity: Sensors, Microcontrollers, Physical Computing, and Participation", "description": "Interactive art joins software to bodies, spaces, objects, and behavior. This unit introduces physical computing and participatory design as ways to make systems that sense and respond.", "children": [{"id": "b6c1b3f2-b4a6-4add-871b-3665006b6dd9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Interaction design for artworks", "children": [{"id": "55b8a3a9-e952-44e6-b48c-364b008de92e", "type": "concept", "title": "Affordances and feedback"}, {"id": "04c7bf03-9340-456a-9c43-99b1ed13da15", "type": "concept", "title": "Input, output, state, and response"}, {"id": "c5b538e2-136d-47e3-bdca-fadb9a3ff8b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Instructions and audience behavior"}, {"id": "1e7120db-c8fd-46b5-9c5c-d089502da517", "type": "concept", "title": "Failure modes and graceful recovery"}], "description": "Students learn how to design encounters, not just mechanisms."}, {"id": "b5b8a1c9-574f-4ea1-96d7-28e98113c8b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sensors and microcontrollers", "children": [{"id": "f8406ff2-f9fe-4fab-816f-08f7a178374d", "type": "concept", "title": "Arduino boards and circuits"}, {"id": "370bc16f-3f82-4b5b-818b-98413c2be5e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Buttons, knobs, light, distance, and motion sensors"}, {"id": "8d67ce4e-79da-418f-aedf-5446052090de", "type": "concept", "title": "LEDs, motors, and displays"}, {"id": "e307a32d-1542-44b9-85aa-746b9ad8cc86", "type": "concept", "title": "Serial communication"}], "description": "Students prototype simple responsive systems using physical inputs and outputs."}, {"id": "49c1b226-2a5d-4cc2-8df8-83d1950bc1a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Participation, consent, and care", "children": [{"id": "3a93e904-62a5-47cc-bbd0-3a57465a4ad7", "type": "concept", "title": "Data capture and consent"}, {"id": "e43bb7c8-7aca-4c23-af89-d799e6860603", "type": "concept", "title": "Accessible interaction"}, {"id": "a3d52873-5a1f-45af-ab45-755a6349c27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Public versus private participation"}, {"id": "eb2898ff-9607-4001-9c6d-444c0870e774", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance during exhibition"}], "description": "Students consider how interactive systems affect bodies, privacy, agency, and access."}]}, {"id": "455e08a5-2231-4baa-b657-34965110cf64", "type": "topic", "title": "3D Modeling, Rendering, Simulation, and Virtual Space", "description": "Three-dimensional digital work gives students tools for sculpture, environment, image-making, animation, fabrication, and immersive worlds. This unit teaches 3D thinking without reducing it to software buttons.", "children": [{"id": "f0cc49c9-a314-4735-a4a1-c3fab3847d7c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Modeling and scene construction", "children": [{"id": "5feb43b0-07f4-47f3-9b82-c6604677cc57", "type": "concept", "title": "Mesh, curve, and primitive modeling"}, {"id": "c7e96f04-eb3a-45d2-a180-4ded815d0938", "type": "concept", "title": "Topology and normals"}, {"id": "1ddf20d0-de4b-44ea-a9a8-c779ae43d19e", "type": "concept", "title": "Scale and units"}, {"id": "1462462a-16af-4786-972a-5ecaeca3dc6b", "type": "concept", "title": "Scene organization"}], "description": "Students learn how objects, surfaces, scale, and spatial relationships are built in digital environments."}, {"id": "b9478fb6-6677-4824-83c8-841ea52fe3b6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Materials, lighting, and rendering", "children": [{"id": "81d4ca59-2fa2-49c5-ab64-ca066a00c562", "type": "concept", "title": "Shaders and materials"}, {"id": "305e2742-ab48-4529-85df-edb5fa6fa586", "type": "concept", "title": "UVs and procedural textures"}, {"id": "35017a7b-aabd-46a4-932e-ad1461e7403d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting setups"}, {"id": "5ec427f5-6d1c-40ef-b5f5-b41b6dfd233e", "type": "concept", "title": "Still and animated renders"}], "description": "Students study how light, surface, texture, and camera settings create atmosphere and meaning."}, {"id": "4d3bde48-0953-420a-9b19-75627e119258", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simulation and virtual sculpture", "children": [{"id": "26724917-365a-4351-af72-497b5359ba07", "type": "concept", "title": "Physics simulation"}, {"id": "a039dc9a-72dd-4c99-8ceb-82f4ffd15f7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Particles and fields"}, {"id": "8e14f434-4cb1-4a26-b934-0f7d9e51f0a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Procedural landscapes"}, {"id": "484137df-d682-4864-aa1a-28da471e8ff8", "type": "concept", "title": "Export for web, game engines, or fabrication"}], "description": "The unit introduces systems that behave over time, from cloth and particles to procedural environments."}]}, {"id": "67e8e0ca-2400-48b0-80c5-a0cc2dd86f6c", "type": "topic", "title": "Game Engines, Real-Time Environments, AR/VR/XR, and Immersive Media", "description": "Real-time media changes the artwork from a fixed output into a responsive world. Students learn how game engines and immersive platforms support spatial storytelling, simulation, performance, and installation.", "children": [{"id": "391d860e-a4f1-4cac-89a4-b614f815272b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Game engine fundamentals", "children": [{"id": "f2219d06-dfbc-4758-9645-c5ff742c046c", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenes, assets, and prefabs"}, {"id": "1f1e8ecf-9109-4c98-97c9-e4d662189c17", "type": "concept", "title": "Cameras, lights, and materials"}, {"id": "7237bf1b-35f0-4116-bc1c-6dc18875d081", "type": "concept", "title": "Physics and collision"}, {"id": "81756c53-83d8-4b4a-af39-7616e069b81d", "type": "concept", "title": "Build settings and deployment"}], "description": "Students learn core concepts that transfer across Unity, Unreal, and similar real-time tools."}, {"id": "f816e4c7-edc4-4458-85ce-d439e1261a4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Worldbuilding and interactive experience", "children": [{"id": "f3293314-f818-4204-af02-f107f6a38638", "type": "concept", "title": "Level and environment design"}, {"id": "fa48154c-d4a2-4738-ac4c-b6d9a5557e5d", "type": "concept", "title": "Navigation and player perspective"}, {"id": "e2505560-d88b-4bf2-a893-d91f8c193c5a", "type": "concept", "title": "Sound and spatial cues"}, {"id": "40c0f474-d6bc-4e5d-9074-21b0f4ea9942", "type": "concept", "title": "Rules, goals, and ambiguity"}], "description": "Students design navigable spaces with mood, pacing, agency, and constraints."}, {"id": "df61fa2f-e8bf-49ae-bddd-954a457288da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AR, VR, XR, and ethics of immersion", "children": [{"id": "9d49ef7b-2a81-490f-ac1b-a57a185e2543", "type": "concept", "title": "Headsets and mobile AR"}, {"id": "90f3c7c9-e93c-4080-a0a1-ba1754da496e", "type": "concept", "title": "Motion comfort and embodiment"}, {"id": "9d3a9e37-dd4a-48df-8e24-403520878ee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Spatial UI"}, {"id": "c5568874-8b91-493e-a598-ed4e73eab51b", "type": "concept", "title": "Safety, surveillance, and presence"}], "description": "The unit frames immersive media as embodied experience with technical, social, and accessibility stakes."}]}, {"id": "7d6a4c81-4cc0-4406-ae03-754b5aa89163", "type": "topic", "title": "Data, Visualization, Machine Vision, AI, and Algorithmic Critique", "description": "Artists increasingly work with datasets, models, sensors, and automated systems. This unit teaches students to use algorithmic tools while questioning what they measure, omit, classify, and amplify.", "children": [{"id": "115e3476-2d00-40cf-8c63-21484fb5687b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data as artistic material", "children": [{"id": "2685cdf4-eca3-42f3-b185-7ebf4370193e", "type": "concept", "title": "Dataset sources and documentation"}, {"id": "9924efc4-b54a-42d6-8c89-bcc0a12042ee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleaning and uncertainty"}, {"id": "2e703ec0-9730-45f7-8915-97cfd7e3559d", "type": "concept", "title": "Mappings from data to image, sound, or motion"}, {"id": "ef79ae23-e5f5-49df-bd37-90fe93d96f4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data feminism and situated knowledge"}], "description": "Students learn to gather, clean, interpret, and transform data into form without pretending data is neutral."}, {"id": "28e1bb0c-e49c-4657-91db-a343775b2273", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Machine vision and AI systems", "children": [{"id": "b584e9c4-9d6d-405e-8c2b-a3d4ea8e9bc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Image classification and detection"}, {"id": "e909ffef-8f98-425e-890c-9265ddc3f3a7", "type": "concept", "title": "Pose and face tracking"}, {"id": "f57acfc8-ff17-460b-83b4-e8aa41b419e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Text-to-image and generative tools"}, {"id": "9d34ae87-2980-417f-a492-70daeb916513", "type": "concept", "title": "Model limits, bias, and hallucination"}], "description": "Students explore computer vision and AI-assisted making as creative tools and cultural objects."}, {"id": "93035d91-2d3e-465b-9e8d-7c3f61abc235", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Algorithmic critique", "children": [{"id": "7e4e362c-6416-4797-ba0c-6def75608e04", "type": "concept", "title": "Bias and representational harm"}, {"id": "112aa7ad-cf77-491b-9211-35b14f77d22d", "type": "concept", "title": "Training data and consent"}, {"id": "ad141116-29a9-4ec0-8541-e8c21fe188ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation and labor"}, {"id": "6aafc408-67f6-48e7-a50b-cf55db182b64", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency, refusal, and counter-design"}], "description": "The goal is to understand computation as power: classification, prediction, sorting, and automation."}]}, {"id": "c6d1449a-e2af-464f-93c0-6ac35133800f", "type": "topic", "title": "Installation, Projection Mapping, Exhibition Design, and Technical Production", "description": "New media works often become real only in space. This unit teaches students to design for walls, rooms, bodies, light, sound, cables, projectors, screens, and gallery operations.", "children": [{"id": "91c1ed5c-5c05-4da3-a974-02f4c12b2358", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition planning and spatial design", "children": [{"id": "99f8cc7d-6b03-4d3d-a9f2-e9a4bf0703a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Floor plans and sightlines"}, {"id": "b406ca03-b76e-4435-bb50-8004db62ca3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Screens, projectors, speakers, and mounts"}, {"id": "e3baadba-1ad4-46d8-9716-bb0f79ac9a3d", "type": "concept", "title": "Audience flow and dwell time"}, {"id": "ee0305eb-fe1b-49bd-a322-f07265be789c", "type": "concept", "title": "Lighting and environmental constraints"}], "description": "Students learn to translate a digital idea into a physical encounter."}, {"id": "18f69e1b-b7ba-480b-a4df-c96ae879f7ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Projection mapping and live media systems", "children": [{"id": "cb137c94-a9fe-4b9a-873d-17a324543d76", "type": "concept", "title": "Projector placement and keystone"}, {"id": "fdf006dd-0c2e-41de-8648-b31cac11a9df", "type": "concept", "title": "Masks and mapping surfaces"}, {"id": "7ce5be09-bc37-4b03-9b62-8a327e64a04d", "type": "concept", "title": "TouchDesigner and real-time routing"}, {"id": "49d369af-3677-4d45-bdf6-d467658c25d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Latency and synchronization"}], "description": "Students explore how images can be aligned to architecture, objects, and performance."}, {"id": "1c422c48-f2f3-420e-92c4-6c750919f04c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Technical production and troubleshooting", "children": [{"id": "4b22cc3a-0d28-40c1-a765-c0d9c3242226", "type": "concept", "title": "Equipment lists and signal flow"}, {"id": "ca0d7b6b-091f-43b7-bdef-17cd87d47e05", "type": "concept", "title": "Cable management and labeling"}, {"id": "55c0c274-3ecd-4591-b572-8f771500ad0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Startup and shutdown procedures"}, {"id": "566dccf5-0869-4601-bdda-e47167976416", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment and backups"}], "description": "The unit builds practical readiness for installing, testing, maintaining, and deinstalling work."}]}, {"id": "5a4b680b-74d4-4375-83cf-32424bbf6770", "type": "topic", "title": "Preservation, Documentation, Accessibility, Copyright, and Platform Ethics", "description": "Digital artworks are fragile because platforms, formats, hardware, and social contexts change. This unit teaches students to document, license, preserve, and present work responsibly.", "children": [{"id": "485c79f9-b53c-4d00-a32a-67e586a586d4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Documentation and preservation strategies", "children": [{"id": "d748b81e-c953-4c94-aa40-36451cc1ab0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Screenshots, video walkthroughs, and source files"}, {"id": "d48ee3f1-a9ab-47d6-8c3e-d1a018940800", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist interviews and installation manuals"}, {"id": "434142ac-944e-47d2-9059-df76a477ed5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration, emulation, and reinterpretation"}, {"id": "5c49b290-5d25-4d2a-b990-6f422f314aac", "type": "concept", "title": "Dependency and version documentation"}], "description": "Students learn to create records that help future viewers, curators, collaborators, and the artist's own archive."}, {"id": "b9047626-d627-43aa-ae2b-72f3709acc6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility and inclusive presentation", "children": [{"id": "d0aad3c2-4f03-491a-9195-29c7954868e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Captions and transcripts"}, {"id": "44fdabf3-dc6e-4a41-9894-2b4fc09dbf1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text and audio description"}, {"id": "04a4b5a1-4352-45c2-8d93-68c52dd2f08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Keyboard and assistive technology support"}, {"id": "52701d46-eda4-4916-b8c5-c5867161de1d", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensory and mobility considerations"}], "description": "The goal is to treat access as part of the artwork's design, not an afterthought."}, {"id": "5acbe57c-01f6-42ba-acb5-65706f1ed0b3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Copyright, licensing, and platform ethics", "children": [{"id": "a598ba6c-0f86-4c8a-9d76-516ad5df0092", "type": "concept", "title": "Fair use and appropriation"}, {"id": "79ea13bb-00c1-4843-9c77-c2f42282cc56", "type": "concept", "title": "Creative Commons licenses"}, {"id": "41371366-3ff2-4f5d-a11a-14f2d37c2c0e", "type": "concept", "title": "Terms of service and platform dependency"}, {"id": "a06b4fbf-82fc-42c9-af2a-342f55d0faf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Privacy, consent, and community standards"}], "description": "Students learn how to use, remix, publish, and protect work with legal and ethical literacy."}]}, {"id": "ac0fe405-7143-4b81-8bdd-ddd44188d5c0", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone New Media Studio: Prototype, Iterate, Critique, Exhibit, and Reflect", "description": "The capstone brings the course together through an ambitious, self-directed project. Students move from proposal to prototype to public presentation, supported by critique, documentation, and reflective writing.", "children": [{"id": "92e10c2a-85c0-4b36-91d8-ba5756be13fd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Project proposal and research", "children": [{"id": "011b8225-ab83-433b-a1ca-09c97be0aaec", "type": "concept", "title": "Concept statement"}, {"id": "28b02c7c-b45f-414c-b0f4-569114deb76f", "type": "concept", "title": "Research precedents"}, {"id": "42144f1c-0b40-4d3e-be0a-08ddefe71844", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical feasibility"}, {"id": "9b2cefdb-22a5-456d-ab74-318feb483975", "type": "concept", "title": "Schedule and materials budget"}], "description": "Students define an artistic question, audience, technical approach, references, and production plan."}, {"id": "d3179c77-fde2-4dab-b282-4528bbcc52eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Prototype and iteration cycle", "children": [{"id": "0ee62cf3-c05a-4cbc-9f1e-f9d232c75c1a", "type": "concept", "title": "Low-fidelity prototypes"}, {"id": "eb408496-bf9d-42f6-afa9-9d7812054cd2", "type": "concept", "title": "User or viewer testing"}, {"id": "486d8b3d-33ae-44aa-8518-6b39782b20ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Critique-based revision"}, {"id": "87ea344d-d4fe-49cf-afe3-c38e1433c2bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Technical problem logs"}], "description": "Students learn to test quickly, critique honestly, and revise based on evidence."}, {"id": "7626369b-9477-42e1-a24a-0e2401a1d02a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exhibition and reflective practice", "children": [{"id": "622fb6f6-dab1-4389-9d96-f9cde07cf471", "type": "concept", "title": "Installation plan"}, {"id": "fdcef5a8-f673-4557-96f0-88f3295fa816", "type": "concept", "title": "Artist statement"}, {"id": "b714e69e-1d99-4b3c-8641-55adb077a42b", "type": "concept", "title": "Process archive"}, {"id": "2344cf30-14dd-4614-a3df-ca8f29c3d204", "type": "concept", "title": "Portfolio-ready documentation"}], "description": "The final work is presented with documentation that explains choices, context, and future development."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$digajson$::jsonb,
